  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1615.02 Grouped Facilities",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1615.02 Grouped Facilities.\n\n(a) If any 2 or more storage facilities are separated from each other by less than the distances specified in Saf-C 1640, then those storage facilities, as a group, shall be considered as one storage facility.\n\n(b) The total quantity of explosive materials stored in such a grouped facility shall be treated as if stored in a single facility and shall comply with the minimum of distances from other storage facilities, inhabited buildings, passenger railways, and public highways, as set forth in Saf-C 1640.\n\nSource. #2220, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2837, eff 8-27-84; ss by #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1600.html"
